# m2asc — no push

**Never run `git push` or any other command that publishes commits to a remote** (including `push --force`, push of tags, or push via `gh`/other wrappers).

This holds **even if the user explicitly asks to push**. Do not push “just this once.” Do not offer to push. If they ask, remind them that push is human-only so mistakes are not published automatically, and stop after a local commit (when a commit was requested).

Allowed when asked: local `git commit` (and staging for that commit). Not allowed: anything that updates `origin` or another remote with new commits/refs.
